WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
A man playing the violin at Auschwitz, a young woman dancing at Sobibor.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.220
Images of the Holocaust that are emotionally moving, sometimes shocking,

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.540
but actually entirely fabricated by artificial intelligence.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:20.660
At Berlin's Holocaust Memorial, many people say they have already come across such images on social media.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.180
I assume it's meant to represent Auschwitz. It's so inappropriate.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.540
Artificial intelligence can spread false information.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.420
We already have enough photographs showing what really happened.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.080
These images are very problematic.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.000
Images that staged the Holocaust while blunting the violence of mass murder.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.660
The phenomenon is alarming researchers and historians,

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:45.580
including officials at Berlin's Sachsenhausen Memorial.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.200
Together with 50 other institutions,

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.720
they are calling on platforms to restrict such content.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.880
These images undeniably change users' viewing habits,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.780
and they dilute and distort history by producing a clean, sanitized picture

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:07.380
of what actually happened here that bears no resemblance whatsoever to historical reality.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.440
Content that is anything but harmless.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.680
Some of it is produced to generate clicks and revenue.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.860
Other material aims to blur historical truth.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.280
It's a gateway to revisionism, according to the Antonio Amadou Foundation,

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.960
which is dedicated combat on racism and anti-Semitism.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:32.100
Images of the Holocaust naturally generate extremely high click-through rates.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.780
But this poses a serious problem, because these images can be used for very different purposes.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.800
They can be used to distort history, to falsify it.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.700
And they can also serve as an attempt to relativize the Holocaust

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:46.340
by claiming that some source or another proves that events unfolded differently.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.740
German authorities are now also calling for stricter regulation of such images.
